# NET-1 pass 2: GNS lanes behind INetTransport (Control / Rpc / Bulk / State) + the connect token in the Hello
# (NET-ARCH §8: {account, server, expiry} signed HMAC-SHA256 with the server secret) + the cook hash read from a
# cooked world directory (Core::CookHashOf of World.dwindex), not a literal.
# The network half runs outside the editor: Tools/DesertNetProbe on loopback, every process at 75 ms one-way send
# lag (150 ms RTT) and 2 % send loss, send rate 1 MB/s; the cooked world is NET-MESH-0's WP_Protocol cook
# (<scratch>/NET-MESH-0/world/WP_Protocol.dwworld). Runner: <scratch>/NET-1/run_net1b.sh; logs <scratch>/NET-1/logs.
#   DesertNetProbe --issue-token --secret-file S --account 1 --server-id 7 --expires-in 600   (A, valid)
#   DesertNetProbe --issue-token --secret-file S --account 2 --server-id 7 --expires-in -60   (B, expired)
#   DesertNetProbe --issue-token --secret-file FORGED --account 3 --server-id 7 --expires-in 600 (C, other key)
#   DesertNetProbe --server --port 27021 --cooked W --server-id 7 --secret-file S --clients 1 --refusals 2
#        --bulk-mb 8 --rpcs 200 --lag-ms 75 --loss 2 --rate-kbps 1024
#   DesertNetProbe --client --connect 127.0.0.1:27021 --cooked W --token <A|B|C> --name A|B|C --lag-ms 75 --loss 2
# Тогда [net1b_lanes_token] server.log: "cook hash ee311acb3b50b349" (or the re-cooked one) read from W; client A
#   accepted (account 1); clientA.log: "bulk 8388608/8388608 bytes in order" and "rpc 200/200" with p95 < 400 ms
#   while the bulk lane was still filling; server.log + clientB.log "token expired", server.log + clientC.log
#   "token invalid"; exit codes A 0, B 2, C 2, server 0.
# The editor is untouched by this pass, but the tree must still build and open the WP world.
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/WP_Protocol.desce
Дано state
Тогда 0_wp_protocol WP_Protocol opens as in dev: landscape, town, sky; no crash or error dialog; no load refusal in editor.log
